   "subject": "camtrapR v3: new functionality + paper in MEE",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Hi everyone,</span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">the <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210x.70409\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210x.70409&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793781065177000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nUA0OJ4JF1qwU0n7xBfgm\">paper describing camtrapR v3</a> has been published in Methods in Ecology and Evolution. </span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">The new package version has been available for a few months already. Since many of you have been using the package for a while, here&#39;s a summary of what&#39;s new. </span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">What&#39;s new in v3</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">----------------</span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">camtrapR started out more than 11 years ago as a tool for preparing camera-trap data for analysis in other packages. V3 now extends it into an end-to-end analytical platform:</span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">- </span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Data import</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">: supported formats now include exports from Wildlife Insights and datasets following the Camtrap DP standard, alongside the classic   camtrapR folder structures.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">- </span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Covariate creation</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">: extract site-level covariates from your own local rasters or from online sources, for use in models and as input for spatial predictions.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">- </span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Exploration</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">: A new function for creating synthetic camera trap data sets for testing. Another function for species accumulation curves.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">- </span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Accessibility</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">: basic camtrapR data objects (camera trap table, record table, camera operation matrix, detection history) now have informative summary() and print() methods, and in some cases plot() methods, providing more meaningful summaries and more in the R console.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">- </span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Community occupancy models</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">: Bayesian community models (via JAGS or NIMBLE) with customizable model structure, and methods for creating response plots and maps of predicted occupancy and species richness, and percentage of area occupied. Convergence diagnostics and posterior predictive checks are available for checking fitted models.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">- </span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">surveyDashboard()</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">: a new graphical interface that walks you through the entire pipeline - data import, exploration, covariates, single species and community occupancy modelling, prediction maps - without writing any code. All tools are available through a graphical interface as a Shiny app. It makes fairly advanced methods more broadly accessible and can be used for analyses of camera-trap analysis as well as teaching without the coding hurdle.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">For a detailed list of changes see the package <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/camtrapR/news/news.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/camtrapR/news/news.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793781065177000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ZOdZnM7OO22Z28atPFMEr\">news section</a>.</span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Getting started</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">---------------</span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Courier New\">install.packages(&quot;camtrapR&quot;)</span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Note that V3 is an addition: existing scripts and workflows continue to work unchanged. New  functionality is covered in <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210x.70409\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210x.70409&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793781065177000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nUA0OJ4JF1qwU0n7xBfgm\">the paper</a></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">. All new functions have help files which you can access via e.g.:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Courier New\">?surveyDashboard</span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">A <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/camtrapR/vignettes/camtrapr6.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/camtrapR/vignettes/camtrapr6.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793781065177000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2NKLUMkzohSEWoVa4hs8Mv\">new vignette</a> (6: Sample camera trap datasets and the &#39;surveyDashboard) loads various sample data sets into the dashboard so you can get a feel for it quickly. </span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Feedback</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">--------</span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">If you run into problems, please post here in the Google Group as usual, or open an <a href=\"https://github.com/jniedballa/camtrapR/issues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jniedballa/camtrapR/issues&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793781065177000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3vNJHfQEt5cxOmpbTNHtDX\">issue on GitHub</a>. </span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">And if there&#39;s functionality you&#39;d like to see, I&#39;d genuinely like to hear about it. Feature requests now have a proper home in the <a href=\"https://github.com/jniedballa/camtrapR/discussions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jniedballa/camtrapR/discussions&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793781065177000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Q3bsptQ18vF6d60ALzMWb\">GitHub discussions</a></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">, but you can also use this Google Group as usual.</span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Thank you for using camtrapR.</span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Best,</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Jürgen Niedballa</span></p>"
    ]
   ]
  }
